// PSS v3.0 LRM — Example 105: state object (page 179)
enum mode_e {...};
state config_s {
rand mode_e mode;
};

13.4 Using flow objects
Flow object references are specified by actions as inputs or outputs. These references are used to specify
rules for combining actions in legal scenarios. An action that outputs a flow object is said to produce that
object and an action that inputs a flow object is said to consume the object. See Syntax 48.
